            <ArticleTitle>Respiratory morbidity in adulthood after respiratory syncytial virus hospitalization in infancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>872-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A prospective &gt;25-year follow-up study evaluated the outcome of patients hospitalized for respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) infection at &lt;24 months of age. Questionnaires were sent to 51 study subjects and to population controls. Self-reported asthma was present in 30% of the former RSV patients, compared with 3.8% of controls. In adjusted analyses, RSV hospitalization was an independent risk factor of adulthood asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
